#
# Component:       repo
# Module:          .env.example
# Owning Team:     Platform Enablement Guild (PEG)
# Classification:  INTERNAL
# Purpose:         Template for the local `.env` read by Docker Compose and the
#                  Makefile. Copy to `.env` and adjust. `.env` is git-ignored;
#                  this file must never contain a real secret.
# Related Docs:    CLAUDE.md (sections 3 "platform at startup", 6.2, 6.3),
#                  compose/README.md

# --- Compose -----------------------------------------------------------------

# Profiles started by `make up` when PROFILES= is not given on the command line.
# `aws-local` is intentionally absent (CLAUDE.md 6.2).
COMPOSE_PROFILES=core,services,frontend,observability

# Build images for the host architecture by default. Set to linux/amd64 to
# cross-build on Apple Silicon when an image lacks an arm64 variant.
# DOCKER_DEFAULT_PLATFORM=linux/amd64

# --- AaaS platform -----------------------------------------------------------

# Environment name sent to config-server (`?env=local`) from step P5.2 on.
AAAS_ENV=local

# Service bootstrap mode (CLAUDE.md section 3):
#   env      — services read configuration from environment variables
#              (the only mode until step P5.2)
#   platform — services fetch configuration from config-server and secrets
#              from OpenBao (available from step P5.3 on)
AAAS_BOOTSTRAP=env

# --- Databases ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-service database credentials are appended here by scripts/new-service.sh
# (step P0.4) in the form <SERVICE>_DB_PASSWORD=change-me. They move to OpenBao
# in step P5.3 and are removed from this file then.
